---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import siteData from "../../content/site.json";
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="Meet Sage and learn about the taste behind Good Intentions.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">Picked and styled by Sage</span>
    <h1>There is no single Good Intentions look.</h1>
    <p>The shop moves between 2000s pop, dreamy layers, festival color, cottagecore, whimsigoth, and whatever else catches Sage's eye. The point is not to fit into one aesthetic. It is to find clothes that make you want to get dressed.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="page-section feature-grid">
    <div class="feature-copy">
      <h2>The common thread is Sage.</h2>
      <p>Collections often begin with a song, a movie, a mood, or one piece that is too good to leave behind. Sage builds from there, mixing secondhand finds into something that feels specific instead of copied from a trend page.</p>
      <p>Good Intentions is also meant to feel approachable. You can shop a piece, ask a question, build a bundle, or talk through an outfit without needing to know the right fashion words first.</p>
      <div class="button-row">
        {siteData.brand.confirmedWords.map((word) => <span class="button button-secondary">{word}</span>)}
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-art"><span>Good clothes.<br />Good vibes.<br />Good intentions.</span></div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
